          %p
            %br/
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dp-D%28p%2B4%29-brane+bound+states"} Dp-D(p+4)-brane bound states
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+instantons"} Yang-Mills instantons
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-D4+brane+bound+state"} D0-D4 brane bound state
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D1-D5+brane+bound+state"} D1-D5 brane bound state
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-D8+brane+bound+state"} D4-D8 brane bound state
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-MO9+brane+bound+state"} M5-MO9 brane bound state
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The first discussion of this compactification is possibly
          %ul
            %li#Sen97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
              , Section 3 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Note on Enhanced Gauge Symmetries in M- and String Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9707123"} arXiv:hep-th/9707123
          %p
            in the context of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+lift+of+gauge+enhancement+on+D6-branes"} M-theory lift of gauge enhancement on D6-branes
          %p The original articles focusing on this situation:
          %ul
            %li#FLO99
              %p
                Michael Faux,
